WEBVTT

00:00:11.503 --> 00:00:12.983
-(SHEEP BLEATING)
-My sheep!

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.263
(BO PEEP EXHALES)

00:00:20.263 --> 00:00:22.303
What did I say?
I lead. You follow.

00:00:22.463 --> 00:00:25.183
Bo, I'm so sorry. Really.
Just tell me how to help.

00:00:25.343 --> 00:00:26.423
You really wanna help?

00:00:26.503 --> 00:00:29.063
Then stay out of my way.
I'm getting my sheep back.

00:00:29.263 --> 00:00:30.263
What about the others?

00:00:30.423 --> 00:00:31.903
Giggle knows what to do.

00:00:35.023 --> 00:00:36.983
MARGARET: Here you go.
GIGGLE: That's our objective.

00:00:37.143 --> 00:00:39.023
We have to get that key.

00:00:39.183 --> 00:00:40.463
It's the only way
inside the cabinet.

00:00:40.663 --> 00:00:41.983
You can't be serious.

00:00:42.063 --> 00:00:43.263
How are we supposed
to do that?

00:00:43.423 --> 00:00:44.703
(LAUGHS) Okay.

00:00:44.863 --> 00:00:46.103
You know what,
leave that to us.

00:00:46.263 --> 00:00:48.223
-We know exactly what to do.
-Mmm-hmm.

00:00:48.303 --> 00:00:50.183
(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)

00:00:50.303 --> 00:00:51.343
Aw.

00:00:51.423 --> 00:00:53.263
Where did you two come from?

00:00:53.423 --> 00:00:55.623
DUCKY: The keys! Give 'em
up now! Where are they?

00:00:55.783 --> 00:00:57.183
Give us the keys!
Give us the keys!

00:00:57.823 --> 00:00:58.903
Well, we're not doing that.

00:00:59.103 --> 00:01:00.183
Yeah, yeah, I agree,
too visible.

00:01:00.263 --> 00:01:01.543
It's a good point.
Something more subtle.

00:01:01.623 --> 00:01:03.103
Ooh, what about "Winner,
winner, chicken dinner"?

00:01:03.183 --> 00:01:04.183
Yes.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.823
DUCKY: The keys! Give 'em
up now! Where are they?

00:01:13.143 --> 00:01:14.943
-Uh... you're kidding.
-Really?

00:01:15.103 --> 00:01:16.623
Okay, okay. You just...

00:01:16.823 --> 00:01:18.023
All right. Well...

00:01:18.103 --> 00:01:20.063
Oh, what about the old
"Plush Rush"?

00:01:20.223 --> 00:01:21.263
There you go!

00:01:21.423 --> 00:01:22.983
(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)

00:01:34.863 --> 00:01:36.503
-Argh. Where is this going?
-Shh! Don't interrupt.

00:01:37.223 --> 00:01:38.863
(SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES)

00:01:46.503 --> 00:01:47.663
(SNORING)

00:01:50.663 --> 00:01:51.663
(MARGARET SCREAMING)

00:01:51.863 --> 00:01:52.983
-Okay, right?
-BUNNY: Uh-huh?

00:01:53.143 --> 00:01:55.223
Not gonna happen.
N-O.

00:01:55.383 --> 00:01:57.063
Okay, do you want
the key or not?

00:01:57.143 --> 00:01:58.343
(GROWLS)
What is wrong with you?

00:01:58.423 --> 00:01:59.423
What is wrong with...?

00:01:59.503 --> 00:02:01.583
We just gave you
three brilliant ideas.

00:02:01.663 --> 00:02:02.983
BUNNY: It's one thing
to say no.

00:02:03.063 --> 00:02:04.663
It's another to offer
a reason...

00:02:04.823 --> 00:02:06.463
How do we get that key?

00:02:11.223 --> 00:02:12.543
(WHISPERING INDISTINCTLY)

00:02:12.623 --> 00:02:14.063
(GASPS) You're kidding!

00:02:14.143 --> 00:02:15.343
(GIGGLES) Really?

00:02:15.503 --> 00:02:16.703
Woody's back?

00:02:16.783 --> 00:02:17.903
(GASPS) Woody's back?

00:02:18.063 --> 00:02:19.863
And you're sure it's Bo Peep
who's with him?

00:02:20.183 --> 00:02:21.303
(BLEATING)

00:02:21.383 --> 00:02:22.383
Thank you, Benson.

00:02:22.543 --> 00:02:23.743
Make sure the others
are ready.

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:25.583
(FORKY EXCLAIMING EXCITEDLY)

00:02:25.663 --> 00:02:26.823
Woody's back!

00:02:27.023 --> 00:02:29.023
I'm coming, Bonnie! (GROANS)

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:30.983
Bonnie.

00:02:31.063 --> 00:02:33.103
First, we must prepare
for his arrival.

00:02:33.263 --> 00:02:34.263
Prepare?

00:02:34.383 --> 00:02:35.503
Have you ever played
hide-and-seek?

00:02:35.663 --> 00:02:37.823
No. But it sounds complicated.

00:02:37.983 --> 00:02:38.983
Oh, it's easy.

00:02:39.143 --> 00:02:40.623
-I'll teach you, okay?
-Okay.

00:02:40.783 --> 00:02:42.343
The first thing you do is...

00:02:42.543 --> 00:02:44.423
one of us finds a place
to hide...

00:02:44.543 --> 00:02:45.503
FORKY: Scary.

00:02:45.623 --> 00:02:46.983
GABBY GABBY: ...while
the other one counts to ten...

00:02:47.063 --> 00:02:48.703
then tries to find them.

00:03:06.703 --> 00:03:08.183
-What are we doing?
-Shh!

00:03:08.423 --> 00:03:11.103
Just stand there and be quiet!

00:03:16.143 --> 00:03:17.983
I'll do the talking.

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:19.143
(TOYS CHEERING)

00:03:19.223 --> 00:03:20.983
Hi, Tinny!

00:03:21.063 --> 00:03:22.783
Aw, nice to see you, too.

00:03:22.863 --> 00:03:23.943
(PLAYS ACCORDION)

00:03:24.023 --> 00:03:25.863
Yeah, he's with me.

00:03:26.023 --> 00:03:27.503
My friend? No, no, no.

00:03:27.703 --> 00:03:29.423
He's my accessory.

00:03:29.703 --> 00:03:31.423
-Hey, guys.
-TOYS: Bo!

00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:33.663
Long time no see.

00:03:33.823 --> 00:03:35.183
Couldn't take it
out there, huh?

00:03:35.263 --> 00:03:36.543
Hey, Doug.
Saw your better half

00:03:36.623 --> 00:03:37.703
at the front of the store.

00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:40.263
Yeah, you mess with the cat,
you get the claws. (CHUCKLES)

00:03:40.343 --> 00:03:41.343
TOY 1: Bo came back!

00:03:41.423 --> 00:03:42.583
TOY 2: Magic 8-Ball was right!

00:03:42.663 --> 00:03:44.703
-Excuse me. Sorry.
-What are you doing here?

00:03:44.783 --> 00:03:46.743
I thought the store
had no return policy!

00:03:46.903 --> 00:03:48.063
ROBOT TOY: Bo, help me out.

00:03:48.143 --> 00:03:49.383
-I need a battery.
-(WOODY CLEARS THROAT)

00:03:49.463 --> 00:03:52.223
VOICE BOX: We got to get
this wagon train a-movin'!

00:03:52.383 --> 00:03:53.703
-Agreed.
-ROBOT TOY: Help, help, help.

00:03:53.783 --> 00:03:54.783
Cheater.

00:03:54.983 --> 00:03:56.103
Have you seen Duke?

00:03:56.263 --> 00:03:57.543
He's in the back.

00:04:05.903 --> 00:04:07.703
Look who jumped
40 school buses

00:04:07.783 --> 00:04:08.983
and landed back into my life.

00:04:09.143 --> 00:04:11.263
-Hi, Duke!
-Who's the cowboy?

00:04:11.343 --> 00:04:13.143
Duke, meet Woody.
Woody, meet...

00:04:13.223 --> 00:04:16.383
Duke Caboom.
Canada's greatest stuntman.

00:04:16.463 --> 00:04:18.023
(GRUNTING) Oh, yeah!

00:04:19.183 --> 00:04:20.343
-Yes!
-WOODY: Huh?

00:04:20.423 --> 00:04:21.903
He's posing.

00:04:22.503 --> 00:04:23.583
Duke?

00:04:23.743 --> 00:04:25.743
-Duke, we need to...
-Hold on. One more.

00:04:25.903 --> 00:04:28.103
Oh, yeah!
What brings you back, Peep?

00:04:28.263 --> 00:04:29.303
We need your help.

00:04:29.463 --> 00:04:32.623
Gabby Gabby has his toy
and my sheep.

00:04:32.783 --> 00:04:35.823
No. Billy, Goat, and Gruff?
Those are my girls.

00:04:36.503 --> 00:04:38.063
What were you doing
getting tangled up

00:04:38.143 --> 00:04:39.503
with Gabby Gabby?
You know better.

00:04:39.663 --> 00:04:42.023
Yeah, some toy thought
it would be a good idea...

00:04:42.183 --> 00:04:43.183
to wander into the aisle.

00:04:43.463 --> 00:04:44.783
That doesn't make any sense.

00:04:44.943 --> 00:04:46.103
It doesn't, does it?

00:04:46.183 --> 00:04:48.543
Everybody knows the best route
is behind the shelves.

00:04:48.703 --> 00:04:50.903
That would have been
a better route, wouldn't it?

00:04:51.063 --> 00:04:52.903
Wow, this toy sounds like
a complete idiot.

00:04:52.983 --> 00:04:54.623
-He does!
-(GROANS)

00:04:54.703 --> 00:04:56.503
Wait, are you that toy?

00:04:57.023 --> 00:04:58.423
So, here's the plan.

00:04:58.583 --> 00:05:01.103
We need to jump over the aisle
to Gabby's cabinet.

00:05:01.263 --> 00:05:03.943
-And you are the toy to do it.
-No.

00:05:04.063 --> 00:05:05.263
-Duke.
-Nope.

00:05:05.343 --> 00:05:06.703
-Duke? Duke?
-Nuh-uh. No way!

00:05:06.783 --> 00:05:08.223
-Duke. Duke!
-Pass. Negative.

00:05:08.383 --> 00:05:09.383
-Duke.
-Rejected.

00:05:09.463 --> 00:05:11.423
Oh, please, Mr. Caboom,
this is really important.

00:05:11.503 --> 00:05:12.543
-My kid...
-(GASPS)

00:05:12.703 --> 00:05:13.703
You have a kid?

00:05:13.863 --> 00:05:15.463
Uh... (CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)

00:05:15.543 --> 00:05:17.983
Hey, Duke, show us some more
poses, what do you say?

00:05:18.143 --> 00:05:20.063
-I had a kid.
-Oh, no.

00:05:20.343 --> 00:05:21.863
Rejean.

00:05:22.023 --> 00:05:25.463
Rejean was so excited when
he got me after Christmas.

00:05:25.863 --> 00:05:28.983
It was the happiest Boxing Day
of my life.

00:05:29.663 --> 00:05:31.103
ANNOUNCER ON TV:
That's Duke Caboom,

00:05:31.183 --> 00:05:33.423
riding the amazing
Caboom stunt cycle!

00:05:33.623 --> 00:05:35.023
Caboom!

00:05:35.743 --> 00:05:38.743
DUKE: I was ready to finally
do what I was made to do.

00:05:38.903 --> 00:05:40.383
ANNOUNCER ON TV: Caboom!

00:05:40.543 --> 00:05:42.383
But when Rejean realized
I couldn't jump

00:05:42.463 --> 00:05:44.023
as far as the toy
in the commercial...

00:05:45.503 --> 00:05:48.263
(GRUNTS) It's a commercial!
It's not real!

00:05:48.423 --> 00:05:49.823
Rejean threw me away!

00:05:49.983 --> 00:05:51.143
It's not fair!

00:05:51.303 --> 00:05:53.183
Why, Rejean? Why?

00:05:53.383 --> 00:05:54.743
(SOBBING)

00:05:54.823 --> 00:05:58.023
Okay, okay.
Calm down, Duke.

00:05:58.183 --> 00:05:59.703
That was a long time ago.

00:06:00.303 --> 00:06:02.103
Right now,
we need the only toy

00:06:02.183 --> 00:06:04.583
who can crash us
onto Gabby's cabinet.

00:06:04.703 --> 00:06:05.663
Crash?

00:06:05.783 --> 00:06:06.783
Crash?

00:06:06.863 --> 00:06:08.903
Any Duke Caboom toy
can land...

00:06:09.063 --> 00:06:12.863
but you are the only one
that can crash the way you do.

00:06:13.023 --> 00:06:14.343
-I am?
-Yes!

00:06:14.663 --> 00:06:16.943
Forget Rejean.
Forget your commercial.

00:06:17.103 --> 00:06:19.343
Be the Duke
you are right now...

00:06:19.503 --> 00:06:22.543
the one who jumps and crashes!

00:06:25.063 --> 00:06:29.583
Be who I am right now.

00:06:30.543 --> 00:06:32.663
Who's the Canuck
with all the luck?

00:06:33.503 --> 00:06:34.503
Caboom?

00:06:34.663 --> 00:06:36.423
Who's the greatest
of the Great White North?

00:06:36.543 --> 00:06:37.543
Caboom!

00:06:37.623 --> 00:06:39.343
Who's the most spectacular
daredevil

00:06:39.423 --> 00:06:40.583
Canada has ever seen?

00:06:40.863 --> 00:06:42.383
Duke Caboom!

00:06:42.783 --> 00:06:43.863
Can you do the jump?

00:06:44.023 --> 00:06:46.063
Yes, I Canada!

00:06:48.023 --> 00:06:49.783
(GRUNTING) Uh-huh.

00:06:49.863 --> 00:06:51.863
-We've got our ride.
-DUKE: Yes!

00:06:52.223 --> 00:06:53.783
VOICE BOX: Yee-haw!

00:06:54.423 --> 00:06:55.503
Yo, Bo!

00:06:55.623 --> 00:06:57.543
Gigs! You made it!

00:06:57.863 --> 00:06:58.943
Good work!

00:06:59.103 --> 00:07:00.263
WOODY: How'd you get it?

00:07:00.703 --> 00:07:02.703
How do we get that key?

00:07:02.783 --> 00:07:04.703
(MARGARET HUMMING)

00:07:08.223 --> 00:07:09.623
-It was hard.
-Very difficult.

00:07:09.783 --> 00:07:11.263
-Barely made it out alive.
-Yeah.

00:07:11.423 --> 00:07:12.463
So, you're welcome.

00:07:12.623 --> 00:07:14.823
Okay. Let's do this.

00:07:15.463 --> 00:07:17.383
Let me wrap that up for you.

00:07:17.543 --> 00:07:20.023
Don't want anything to happen
to it on the way home.

00:07:20.183 --> 00:07:22.343
Good. That sale buys us
some time.

00:07:23.463 --> 00:07:24.623
Wait for it.

00:07:27.023 --> 00:07:28.703
All right, let's go!

00:07:42.023 --> 00:07:43.183
(GRUNTING)

